<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chinese New Year</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Spring Festival, Lunar New Year, Chūnjié, 春節</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chinese New Year, also known as the Spring Festival, marks the beginning of a new year on the traditional lunisolar Chinese calendar, on the new moon that falls between 21 January and 20 February. The festival runs from New Year's Eve, when families gather for the reunion dinner, to the Lantern Festival on the 15th day of the year. Records of the first celebration can be traced to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warring-states-period">Warring States period</a> (475–221 BCE). Houses are cleaned, doors are decorated with red couplets, firecrackers are lit and money is given in red envelopes. It has influenced other new year celebrations, among them the Tết of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, the Seollal of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> and the Losar of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chinese-new-year.jpg" alt="Chinese New Year" width="330" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Myrabella · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nouvel_an_chinois_2015_Paris_13_autel.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Chinese New Year</b> is still set by the traditional lunisolar calendar.</blockquote><a href="/essays/midwinter">Midwinter</a></li><li><blockquote>It carries the New Year song &quot;Xīnnián Hǎo&quot;, sung at <b>Chinese New Year</b>, the Jewish New Year song &quot;Dip the Apple in the Honey&quot;, &quot;Yeh Hai Bombay Meri Jaan&quot; in the Hindi film C.I.D. (1956), the Indonesian children's song &quot;Makan Apa&quot; and a drinking song of Scandinavian student…</blockquote><a href="/songs/oh-my-darling-clementine">Oh My Darling, Clementine</a></li></ul></section>
